1.3 The GB APU shim (audio/shim/)

    The SPC700 program that models the Game Boy's sound hardware, and its
    encoders (shim.bin, shim_abi.inc, shimpkg.zig, wave.zig, noise.zig). It is
    James Schurig's own code, generated in his snes_game_dev repository at the
    commit audio/shim/MANIFEST names (3924c36a1a59396b51089c59c61fee77df89983f)
    and copied here. That repository has no licence file. Its author licenses
    this copy under this repository's MIT licence (LICENSE).

    Its sources were read for third-party code before release. None was found.
    The shim's register definitions (audio/gbapu/registers.inc there) were
    written out from hardware documentation, deliberately not taken from the
    Terrific Audio Driver's zlib-licensed equivalent. The shim follows that
    driver's coding style only. Its output level is set to match SameBoy's
    rendering of the Game Boy, but no SameBoy code is in it.


2. Used at development time only (not in the binary)
----------------------------------------------------

None of these is committed to this repository. Each is fetched by a script in
tools/ into the ignored vendor/ or reference/ directories, under its own licence.

- SameBoy (Expat/MIT, Copyright (c) 2015-2025 Lior Halphon),
  https://github.com/LIJI32/SameBoy. Reference frames for grading the PPU, and
  the reference player behind `zig build audioab` (src/sbref.c links its APU).
- M2RoS (MIT, above), fetched by tools/get-bank4-sym.sh to name bank 4's
  routines in `zig build audiocost`.
- Vashy777/metroid2 (MIT), https://github.com/Vashy777/metroid2. An mgbdis dump,
  used for the routine inventory behind `zig build ledger`.
- asar (LGPL-3.0-or-later), https://github.com/RPGHacker/asar. Assembles
  engine/main.asm into the committed engine/engine.bin. Its author claims no
  copyright over its output.
- spc700asm, from the Terrific Audio Driver (compiler: MIT; Copyright (c) 2023
  Marcus Rowe), https://github.com/undisbeliever/terrific-audio-driver.
  Assembles engine/audio/main.asm into the committed engine/audio.bin.
- Blargg's Game Boy test ROMs, via https://github.com/retrio/gb-test-roms, for
  the emulator's CPU tests.
- Tool-assisted movies from https://tasvideos.org, replayed by `zig build tas`.
